      "question_id": "DGF-EXPLAIN-005",
      "status": "answered",
      "summary": "C_MEETING_WEAK remains source-supported and allowed by the ordered Sato plus weak-commitment witness, while grounded K_MEETING_NOT_WEAK separately derives that the Tanaka plus weak-commitment pair is forbidden.",
      "evidence": [
        "MEETING_WEAK_EXPLAIN_JSON reports support supported, viability allowed, the joint assignments V_MEETING_ACTOR=C_MEETING_SATO and V_MEETING_COMMITMENT=C_MEETING_WEAK, and all three meeting constraint IDs.",
        "MEETING_EXCLUDES_EXPLAIN_JSON reports typed excludes operands C_MEETING_TANAKA and C_MEETING_WEAK plus RCG-RSN-202 grounded through S_ADR_MINIMAL_MEETING and S_PROV_EXCLUSION_CHAIN."
      ]
    },
    {
      "question_id": "DGF-EXPLAIN-006",
      "status": "answered",
      "summary": "C_FIXED_WEAK retains positive explicit support while viability is excluded; explain and audit report RCG-CSP-002 without changing support to conflicted.",
      "evidence": [
        "SUPPORTED_EXCLUDED_EXPLAIN_JSON reports support supported, viability excluded, RCG-RSN-201/202/206, and applies(C_FIXED_WEAK,K_FIXED_NOT_WEAK).",
        "Its RCG-CSP-002 names K_FIXED_ACTOR and K_FIXED_NOT_WEAK, and DOCUMENT_AUDIT_JSON repeats that finding while preserving support and viability as separate projections."
      ]
    },
    {
      "question_id": "DGF-EXPLAIN-007",
      "status": "answered",
      "summary": "V_CONFLICT_LEFT and V_CONFLICT_RIGHT are the two closed variables with no satisfying represented world, and audit reports them deterministically before the supported-but-excluded warnings.",
      "evidence": [
        "DOCUMENT_AUDIT_JSON reports RCG-CSP-001 for V_CONFLICT_LEFT then V_CONFLICT_RIGHT, each naming K_CONFLICT_LEFT, K_CONFLICT_RIGHT, and K_CONFLICT_PAIR.",
        "The complete non-truncated audit reports two errors and three warnings, fails the error threshold, and does not invent an unspecified candidate or weaken a closure."
      ]
    },
    {
      "question_id": "DGF-EXPLAIN-008",
      "status": "answered",
      "summary": "With limit 1, C_LIMIT_B1 remains unknown because the first represented pair is blocked and the next pair cannot be inspected; both repetitions report the same incomplete result rather than false or excluded.",
      "evidence": [
        "LIMIT_UNKNOWN_EXPLAIN_JSON reports viability unknown and variable resolution unknown with RCG-RSN-007, complete false, truncated true, and exit status 1.",
        "Both repetitions have identical stdout digest sha256:f0f8f926fdc9429fb44064cb97ce76b469d675573c131c36ae63a2ef52271ce8 and retain RCG-RSN-202 for the attempted C_LIMIT_A1 plus C_LIMIT_B1 pair."
      ]
